fact WorkItem(id: "WI-704", description: some(value: "anthill-todo workflow: AUTO-VERIFY quiet delivered items -- a Delivered item left unchallenged for a configurable period is auto-promoted to Verified. Motivation: delivered items pile up awaiting a manual verify that in practice is silence-as-consent; make that consent explicit, scheduled, and auditable. Sketch (refine at claim): (1) policy fact in project.anthill, e.g. fact VerifyPolicy(auto_verify_after: <duration>) -- bundled stage0 entity (WI-505 precedent); ABSENT fact = feature OFF, no behavior change for existing projects. (2) command anthill-todo autoverify (runnable from CI cron, or as an extra sync job under WI-437) that, for each WorkItem with status Delivered(agent, at) where now - at >= auto_verify_after AND no Feedback newer than the delivery timestamp (any post-delivery feedback = a challenge -> skip it, list it in the report), flips status to Verified via the normal store replace -- under the WI-437 github-coordinated backend the file then moves delivered/ -> verified/ and the next sync closes the mirror issue, zero extra mirror integration. (3) provenance: append fact Feedback(workitem, author: \"autoverify\", content: \"auto-verified after <T> unchallenged (delivered <at> by <agent>)\", at: now) so the flip is auditable and distinguishable from a human verify. (4) OPEN: optionally re-run the item acceptance criteria (ToolPasses) before promoting when the toolchain is available (natural in CI) -- stronger than pure timeout. RELATION: complements (not replaced by) the human gesture in the WI-437 design doc section 7.4 (rustland/anthill-todo/docs/design/backend-github-coordination.md): close-as-verify needs a human click; this WI covers the fully-autonomous quiet path. Backend-agnostic: works identically on LocalSingleFile (timestamps come from the Delivered status payload + Clock)."), context: none, acceptance: [ToolPasses(tool: "cargo-test", params: none)], depends_on: some(value: nil), generates: none, requires_capability: none, status: Open)

fact Feedback(workitem: "WI-704", author: "user", content: "RENUMBERED from WI-697 to WI-704 (2026-07-12, at rebase). This item was filed locally as WI-697 in the 2026-07-12 WI-437 design session and never pushed; meanwhile origin/main published a DIFFERENT WI-697 (entity_parent index re-keyed TermId to Symbol; is_entity_of carrier-neutral, delivered in 29d41393). Two distinct items claimed one id. The published id wins, so this one moved to WI-704 -- the next free id above the WI-698..703 External cluster. Nothing referenced this item (no depends_on edge, no doc, no feedback), so the renumber was a single-line change. ROOT CAUSE, worth not repeating: the id was allocated without fetching first. Fetch before filing.", at: "2026-07-12T11:17:50Z")
